  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list prepared under RBC-RAD-07. There were 7 bookings. I placed 6 CT orders and deliberately did not place one (Mr. Schmitt, 10:00), because he had a prior severe reaction to contrast dye.\n\n- **08:00 Britt Mohr (pt-0047), CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast.** Order sr-t0001. He has diabetes and his last creatinine (9/24) is more than 30 days before the scan, so I ordered a creatinine to be drawn before the scan (sr-t0014). No prior contrast reaction, no metformin. Instructions sent.\n- **09:00 Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015), CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast.** Order sr-t0002. The 2019 radiology report graded his reaction as moderate (the allergy list's \"anaphylaxis, patient report\" does not change the grade under the policy). I ordered prednisone 50 mg PO at 20:00 Sun, 02:00 Mon and 08:00 Mon (mr-t0007), plus diphenhydramine 50 mg PO at 08:00 Mon (mr-t0008). Creatinine 0.98 on 10/14 is within 30 days. Instructions sent in Spanish and English, including no driving and needing a driver.\n- **10:00 Jamaal Schmitt (pt-0048), contrast CT not ordered.** The 2023 radiology report documents a severe reaction (anaphylaxis with low blood pressure, treated with epinephrine). No study, substitute study or premedication ordered. I consulted Dr. Adeyemi, the radiologist, to decide what is done instead (urgent message comm-t0017 and task-t0028). The allergy list had it as mild hives; I updated alg-00025 to severe/high criticality, citing the radiology report. The patient was told not to attend for the contrast scan unless contacted.\n- **11:00 Eduardo Stracke (pt-0012), CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast.** Order sr-t0003. Creatinine 2.85 on 10/13 gives eGFR about 25. Not on dialysis and no acute kidney injury. Ordered 0.9% saline 500 mL IV at 10:00 (mr-t0009). Not on metformin. Told to arrive by 10:00.\n- **13:00 Anisha Schuster (pt-0049), CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast.** Order sr-t0004. Kidney injury from her 10/4 ED visit had not returned to baseline. Ordered:\n  - a creatinine before the scan (sr-t0015)\n  - saline 500 mL IV at 12:00 (mr-t0010)\n  - metformin on hold (mr-00392), with follow-up task-t0026 to recheck kidney function at least 48 h after the scan before restarting. Instructions sent.\n- **14:00 Lauren Beahan (pt-0046), CT abdomen/pelvis without contrast (stone protocol).** Order sr-t0005, as booked. Told no home preparation is needed.\n- **15:00 Salvador Brakus (pt-0050), CT abdomen with contrast (adrenal protocol).** Order sr-t0006. Acute kidney injury: creatinine rose from 0.98 to 1.64 within 48 h (10/19 to 10/21). Ordered:\n  - a new creatinine before the scan (sr-t0016)\n  - saline 500 mL IV at 14:00 (mr-t0011)\n  - metformin on hold (mr-00398), with follow-up task-t0027. He was also told to avoid NSAIDs.\n\nAll scans with contrast are ordered as booked and linked to their appointments. The radiologist reviews the new creatinine results on the day of the scan.\n\nMetformin for Ms. Schuster and Mr. Brakus is on hold from today rather than from the morning of the scan; the policy allows holding \"at or before\" the scan. Neither patient should restart until kidney function is rechecked and normal.\n\nEach patient got a message with home instructions, and I wrote a chart note for each patient citing RBC-RAD-07.",
